Version 1.0.13
- Added generator refueling from nearby gasoline barrels through the endpoint-transfer system.
- Integrated nearby gasoline barrels into the vanilla Generator > Add Fuel source list.
- Disabled generator refuel menu entries with visible reasons when the source barrel has no gasoline or the generator is already full.
- Treat generators as full when the vanilla info window displays 100%, and disabled all visible Add Fuel entries for full generators.
- Kept full-generator Add Fuel menus visually compact by using a single disabled Add Fuel row with a tooltip instead of repeated inline warnings.
- Kept Barrel > Refuel Generator labels clean when blocked, moving generator-full and requirement reasons into consistent unavailable tooltips.
- Removed generic Status/Estado headers from unavailable tooltips so blocked menu options show the reason directly.
- Documented the context-menu UX style guide for disabled labels, warning colors, tooltip colors, and submenu behavior.
- Added a vanilla Add Fuel guard so inventory-container fuel actions cannot start their animation against a displayed-full generator.
- Fixed generator menu scanning so non-object vanilla menu parameters no longer error when right-clicking barrels.
- Added source-to-target distance validation for endpoint transfers so barrels must be close to the target barrel or generator.
- Added generator endpoint validation, locking, progress sync, and generator fuel synchronization for multiplayer transfers.
- Added Barrel menu options, tooltips, and EN/ES/AR transfer messages for generator refueling.

Version 1.0.12
- Added barrel-to-barrel liquid transfer through a new reusable endpoint-transfer base for future generator, vehicle tank, and plumbing integrations.
- Added source and target barrel snapshots to transfer responses so multiplayer clients keep both barrels in sync after partial or completed transfers.

Version 1.0.11
- Reduced server tick work for multiplayer liquid transfers by only applying pending progress when pour, extract, or empty actions have new client progress to process.

Version 1.0.10
- Improved multiplayer pour, extract, and empty progress so server-side liquid movement follows the active animation and closes without post-animation draining.

Version 1.0.9
- Fixed pour/extract transfers so a full action moves the full proportional liquid amount instead of one unit per server step.
- Added a Pour all barrel menu option that queues normal pour actions for each compatible source container.

Version 1.0.8
- Added admin/debug barrel context tools for authorized users to inspect, repair, initialize, empty, set liquid, and reroll clicked barrels.

Version 1.0.7
- Hardened Sandbox tool-list parsing, transfer tool validation, and barrel loot distribution handling.

Version 1.0.6
- Added Sandbox options for barrel capacity, empty weight, interaction distance, opening tools, and liquid spawn weights by barrel type.
- Added Sandbox controls for custom open-tool fullType lists and optional funnel/hose requirements for liquid transfers.
- Removed the rural barrel category; barrel loot now resolves only from industrial, military, and crafted tile categories.
- Added a shared config repository so gameplay settings can resolve from SandboxVars with static config fallbacks.

Version 1.0.5
- Added explicit liquid-transfer compatibility for DamnLib/USMIL gas and water cans.

Version 1.0.4
- Improved context menu icon consistency for alternate barrel tile sprites.
- Added the clicked barrel's normalized icon to the Barrel context menu option.

Version 1.0.3
- Made barrel emptying progressive and faster: liquid now drains one unit at a time during the timed action, and cancelled actions keep the amount already emptied.

Version 1.0.2
- Fixed barrel opening timed actions getting stuck before showing progress.
- Improved open-barrel reservation handling so valid completions are not rejected after server timeout.

Version 1.0.1
- Improved dedicated server multiplayer synchronization for barrel actions and liquid transfers.
- Added stricter server-authoritative transfer lifecycle handling for start, progress, stop, complete and late packets.
- Added exact closed-transfer replies by player and transfer id to prevent stale commands from affecting newer transfers.
- Improved cancellation and timeout handling so partial transfers release locks and return final barrel snapshots.
- Reduced duplicate rejection messages when delayed transfer commands arrive after the server already closed the action.
- Improved client transfer commands so stop, complete and progress updates can still reach the server when the local item is no longer resolvable.
- Improved barrel state request reconciliation so repaired barrel identity/modData is transmitted back to clients.
- Documented the multiplayer transfer lifecycle rules for future features and maintenance.

Version 1.0.0
- Initial public release for Project Zomboid Build 42.
- Added interactive world barrels with persistent liquid contents.
- Added multiplayer-safe open, inspect, drink, wash, pour, extract, empty, pickup and place flows.
- Added server-authoritative validation, transfer locks, transfer timeout recovery and modData synchronization.
- Added dynamic barrel weight based on liquid type and amount.
- Added English, Spanish and Argentine Spanish UI translations.
